    "scope": "The indexed lines call the supplied RowT theorem and take its local projections. The contragredient identification and existence of a weak correspondence enter separately in the consumer."
  },
  "retained_inputs": [
    "B9.02 gives its conclusion for each correspondence satisfying B9.47–49. Existence of such a correspondence is B9.46.",
    "Chebotarev density and Brauer–Nesbitt in characteristic zero identify continuous semisimple representations. The parallel infinity exponent uses Dirichlet’s unit theorem.",
    "The ramified comparison uses class field theory, cuspidal genericity for GL_a, and the rank, segment, type and determinant laws of the specified weak correspondence.",
    "GERK1–3 use the geometric and local hypotheses of B9.39–41, the auxiliary-character theorem B9.36c and odd-rank attachment for the lifted definite unitary forms. The B9.38 proof in GSPH6 uses the published theorem over the CM field."
  ]
